613 0 obj<</Title(1. Estimated cost for materials shall include quotes from multiple sources. Material prices shall include applicable fees and credits, including but not limited to, sales tax, freight and delivery charges, and tax rebates.)/Parent 612 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[381 0 R/XYZ 69 139 0]>>/Next 614 0 R>>
endobj
614 0 obj<</Title(2. No markup shall be applied to any material provided by NPS.)/Parent 612 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[381 0 R/XYZ 69 89 0]>>/Prev 613 0 R>>
endobj
616 0 obj<</Title(D. Equipment:)/Parent 601 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 720 0]>>/Prev 612 0 R/First 617 0 R/Last 629 0 R/Count 10/Next 630 0 R>>
endobj
617 0 obj<</Title(1. The equipment used for the project must be appropriately sized for work being performed.)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 707 0]>>/Next 618 0 R>>
endobj
618 0 obj<</Title(2. Do not include costs for "miscellaneous tools and equipment", in your proposal for a replacement value of $500 or less. Costs shown in excess of $500 shall be broken out separately.)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 670 0]>>/Prev 617 0 R/Next 619 0 R>>
endobj
619 0 obj<</Title(3. Regardless of ownership, rates to be used in determining equipment rental costs shall be the lowest cost from one of the following sources:)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 632 0]>>/Prev 618 0 R/First 620 0 R/Last 622 0 R/Count 3/Next 623 0 R>>
endobj
620 0 obj<</Title(a. United States \(U.S.\) Army Corps of Engineers, Ownership and Operating Expense Schedule \(use latest edition and applicable region\))/Parent 619 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 606 0]>>/Next 621 0 R>>
endobj
621 0 obj<</Title(b. Construction Blue Book)/Parent 619 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 569 0]>>/Prev 620 0 R/Next 622 0 R>>
endobj
622 0 obj<</Title(c. Local equipment rental rates, documented by actual invoice charges, or itemized vendor quotes.)/Parent 619 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 556 0]>>/Prev 621 0 R>>
endobj
623 0 obj<</Title(4. Estimated equipment rates shall include operating costs of all fuel, oil, lubrication, supplies, small tools, necessary attachments, ground engaging components, tires and tracks, routine repairs and maintenance \(cost of major repair and overhaul is...)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 531 0]>>/Prev 619 0 R/Next 624 0 R>>
endobj
624 0 obj<</Title(5. Estimate full rate for equipment only for duration that equipment will be utilized to accomplish work of the modification.)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 443 0]>>/Prev 623 0 R/Next 625 0 R>>
endobj
625 0 obj<</Title(6. Standby unit rates used in accordance with paragraph 1.3, D, 2, above. If the U.S. Army Corp of Engineers is utilized, then their standby rates prevail. If Bluebook or local equipment pricing is accepted, then 1/2 of equipment costs minus any opera...)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 418 0]>>/Prev 624 0 R/Next 626 0 R>>
endobj
626 0 obj<</Title(7. If equipment is in standby mode due solely to a documented NPS delay, established standby rate shall apply from the first day of the delay.)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 367 0]>>/Prev 625 0 R/Next 627 0 R>>
endobj
627 0 obj<</Title(8. Equipment not used and on the job site for up to five consecutive days may be classified at standby rates, provided the equipment is or has been used solely to perform work on the modification and will be necessary to complete additional modificati...)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 342 0]>>/Prev 626 0 R/Next 628 0 R>>
endobj
628 0 obj<</Title(9. Requests for compensation for equipment stand by time must be justified, documented and itemized separately.)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 279 0]>>/Prev 627 0 R/Next 629 0 R>>
endobj
629 0 obj<</Title(10. The estimated timeframe \(daily, weekly, monthly\) for use of the equipment must reflect the lowest cost to the Government.)/Parent 616 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 253 0]>>/Prev 628 0 R>>
endobj
630 0 obj<</Title(E. Establishment and Application of Overhead and Profit Percentages:)/Parent 601 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 69 228 0]>>/Prev 616 0 R/First 631 0 R/Last 636 0 R/Count 5>>
endobj
631 0 obj<</Title(1. Home Office Overhead and Profit \(OH&P\) shall be applied to direct costs only. Profit shall not be applied to overhead amounts; and overhead shall not be applied to profit.  Home office overhead shall contain only allowable, allocable, and reasonabl...)/Parent 630 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[384 0 R/XYZ 157 203 0]>>/Next 633 0 R>>
endobj
633 0 obj<</Title(2. Total aggregate limit of markup \(OH&P\) for Contractor and Subcontractors on modification work shall not exceed 25%. The NPS will not be responsible for allocation of percentages between contractor and subcontractors at any tier.)/Parent 630 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[386 0 R/XYZ 69 720 0]>>/Prev 631 0 R/Next 634 0 R>>
endobj
634 0 obj<</Title(3. If Contractors form a partnership, partnership may only receive home office overhead and profit in same amount as an individual Contractor \(refer to paragraph 1.3,E,1 above\). It is the responsibility of the partners to decide on division of revenue.)/Parent 630 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[386 0 R/XYZ 69 682 0]>>/Prev 633 0 R/Next 635 0 R>>
endobj
635 0 obj<</Title(4. Combined Increases and Decreases: On proposals involving both increases and decreases in the Contract Price, overhead and profit mark-ups are required on net increases and deducted on net decreases.)/Parent 630 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[386 0 R/XYZ 69 644 0]>>/Prev 634 0 R/Next 636 0 R>>
endobj
636 0 obj<</Title(5. At no time can profit be calculated on Overhead or itself, it must be calculated on direct costs of work only.)/Parent 630 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[386 0 R/XYZ 69 606 0]>>/Prev 635 0 R>>
endobj
637 0 obj<</Title(PART 2 -  PRODUCTS)/Parent 512 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[386 0 R/XYZ 69 580 0]>>/Prev 514 0 R/Next 638 0 R>>
endobj
638 0 obj<</Title(PART 3 -  EXECUTION)/Parent 512 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[386 0 R/XYZ 69 544 0]>>/Prev 637 0 R>>
endobj
