2550 0 obj<</Title(1.2 DEFINITIONS)/Parent 2537 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2340 0 R/XYZ 69 424 0]>>/Prev 2538 0 R/First 2551 0 R/Last 2567 0 R/Count 13/Next 2568 0 R>>
endobj
2551 0 obj<</Title(A. "Preservation" - To apply measures necessary to sustain existing form, integrity, and materials of historic property. Work may include preliminary measures to protect and stabilize the property.)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2340 0 R/XYZ 112 387 0]>>/Next 2552 0 R>>
endobj
2552 0 obj<</Title(B. "Rehabilitation" - To make possible a compatible use for property through repair, alterations, and additions while preserving those portions or features that convey its historical, cultural, or architectural values.)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2340 0 R/XYZ 112 350 0]>>/Prev 2551 0 R/Next 2553 0 R>>
endobj
2553 0 obj<</Title(C. "Restoration" - To accurately return form, features, and character of a property to its appearance at a particular period of time by means of removal of features from other periods in its history and repair and reconstruction of missing and deterio...)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2340 0 R/XYZ 69 300 0]>>/Prev 2552 0 R/Next 2554 0 R>>
endobj
2554 0 obj<</Title(D. "Reconstruction" - To reproduce in exact form and detail, a building, structure, or artifact as it appeared at a specific period in time. Reconstructed elements do not possess historic integrity in their own right since they are not original fabric.)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2340 0 R/XYZ 69 250 0]>>/Prev 2553 0 R/Next 2555 0 R>>
endobj
2555 0 obj<</Title(E. "Stabilize" - To apply measures designed to reestablish a weather-resistant enclosure and structural reinforcement of an item or portion of the building while maintaining essential form as it exists at present. This level of intervention is aimed a...)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2340 0 R/XYZ 112 200 0]>>/Prev 2554 0 R/Next 2556 0 R>>
endobj
2556 0 obj<</Title(F. "Protect and Maintain" - To remove deteriorating corrosion, reapply protective coatings, and install protective measures such as temporary guards; to provide the least degree of intervention.)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2340 0 R/XYZ 69 137 0]>>/Prev 2555 0 R/Next 2558 0 R>>
endobj
2558 0 obj<</Title(G. "Repair" - To stabilize, consolidate, or conserve; to retain existing materials and features while employing as little new material as possible. Repair includes patching, piecing-in, splicing, consolidating, or otherwise reinforcing or upgrading ma...)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2356 0 R/XYZ 69 720 0]>>/Prev 2556 0 R/Next 2559 0 R>>
endobj
2559 0 obj<</Title(H. "Replace" - To duplicate in its entirety, a historic element or feature by matching its historic pattern, detail and appearance. Replacement is justified when original or historic elements are damaged beyond repair or are missing. Replacement condi...)/Parent 2550 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2356 0 R/XYZ 69 644 0]>>/Prev 2558 0 R/First 2560 0 R/Last 2562 0 R/Count 3/Next 2563 0 R>>
endobj
2560 0 obj<</Title(1. Replacement with Original or Historic Fabric: Includes fabric salvaged from other locations or projects having identical architectural qualities. Duplication of appearance using identical material possessing historical significance.)/Parent 2559 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2356 0 R/XYZ 69 594 0]>>/Next 2561 0 R>>
endobj
2561 0 obj<</Title(2. Replacement with New Materials: Includes replacement with new material of like kind \(custom fabricated of manufactured\). Duplication of appearance using like material.)/Parent 2559 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2356 0 R/XYZ 69 544 0]>>/Prev 2560 0 R/Next 2562 0 R>>
endobj
