2671 0 obj<</Title(3.4 PROTECTION DURING USE OF HEAT-GENERATING EQUIPMENT)/Parent 2632 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 507 0]>>/Prev 2662 0 R/First 2672 0 R/Last 2685 0 R/Count 2/Next 2686 0 R>>
endobj
2672 0 obj<</Title(A. Comply with following procedures while performing work with heat-generating equipment, including welding, cutting, soldering, brazing, paint removal with heat, and other operations where open flames or implements utilizing heat are used:)/Parent 2671 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 112 470 0]>>/First 2673 0 R/Last 2683 0 R/Count 8/Next 2685 0 R>>
endobj
2673 0 obj<</Title(1. Obtain Contracting Officer\220s approval for operations involving use of open-flame or welding equipment.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 420 0]>>/First 2674 0 R/Last 2675 0 R/Count 2/Next 2676 0 R>>
endobj
2674 0 obj<</Title(a. Notification shall be given for each occurrence and location of work with heat-generating equipment.)/Parent 2673 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 383 0]>>/Next 2675 0 R>>
endobj
2675 0 obj<</Title(b. Obtain appropriate permit from the park as required.)/Parent 2673 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 346 0]>>/Prev 2674 0 R>>
endobj
2676 0 obj<</Title(2. As far as practical, use heat-generating equipment in shop areas or outside building.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 333 0]>>/Prev 2673 0 R/Next 2677 0 R>>
endobj
2677 0 obj<</Title(3. Before work with heat-generating equipment commences, furnish fire watch \(or watches\) for location\(s\) where work is to be performed.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 309 0]>>/Prev 2676 0 R/Next 2678 0 R>>
endobj
2678 0 obj<</Title(4. Do not perform work with heat-generating equipment in or near rooms or in areas where flammable liquids or explosive vapors are present or thought to be present. Use combustible gas indicator test to ensure area is safe.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 283 0]>>/Prev 2677 0 R/Next 2679 0 R>>
endobj
2679 0 obj<</Title(5. Remove and keep area free of combustibles, including, rubbish, paper, waste, etc., within area of operations.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 245 0]>>/Prev 2678 0 R/First 2680 0 R/Last 2680 0 R/Count 1/Next 2681 0 R>>
endobj
2680 0 obj<</Title(a. If combustible material cannot be removed, provide fireproof blankets to cover such materials.)/Parent 2679 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 220 0]>>>>
endobj
2681 0 obj<</Title(6. Where possible, furnish and use baffles of metal or gypsum board to prevent spraying of sparks or hot slag into surrounding combustible material.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 183 0]>>/Prev 2679 0 R/Next 2682 0 R>>
endobj
2682 0 obj<</Title(7. Prevent extension of sparks and particles of hot metal through open windows, doors, holes, and cracks in floors, walls, ceilings, roofs, and other openings.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 145 0]>>/Prev 2681 0 R/Next 2683 0 R>>
endobj
2683 0 obj<</Title(8. Inspect each location of day's work not sooner than 30 minutes after completion of operations to detect hidden or smoldering fires; ensure proper housekeeping is maintained.)/Parent 2672 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2373 0 R/XYZ 69 120 0]>>/Prev 2682 0 R>>
endobj
2685 0 obj<</Title(B. Where sprinkler protection exists and is functional, maintain without interruption while operations are performed. If operations are performed near automatic sprinkler heads, shield individual heads temporarily with guards.)/Parent 2671 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 720 0]>>/Prev 2672 0 R>>
endobj
2686 0 obj<</Title(3.5 HISTORIC PRESERVATION TREATMENT PROCEDURES)/Parent 2632 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 682 0]>>/Prev 2671 0 R/First 2687 0 R/Last 2697 0 R/Count 10>>
endobj
2687 0 obj<</Title(1. Retain as much existing material as possible; repair and consolidate rather than replace.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 570 0]>>/Next 2688 0 R>>
endobj
2688 0 obj<</Title(2. Use additional material or structure to reinforce, strengthen, prop, tie, and support existing material or structure.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 546 0]>>/Prev 2687 0 R/Next 2689 0 R>>
endobj
2689 0 obj<</Title(3. Use reversible processes wherever possible.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 520 0]>>/Prev 2688 0 R/Next 2690 0 R>>
endobj
2690 0 obj<</Title(4. Use traditional replacement materials and techniques if possible. New work shall be distinguishable from old work and original materials and techniques.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 508 0]>>/Prev 2689 0 R/Next 2691 0 R>>
endobj
2691 0 obj<</Title(5. Record repair work during construction with periodic construction photos and daily inspection reporting. Photo documentation is specified in Section 013233 "Photographic Documentation.")/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 482 0]>>/Prev 2690 0 R/Next 2692 0 R>>
endobj
2692 0 obj<</Title(B. Prohibit smoking by personnel performing work on or near historic structures.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 444 0]>>/Prev 2691 0 R/Next 2693 0 R>>
endobj
2693 0 obj<</Title(C. Notify Contracting Officer of visible changes in integrity of material or components due to environmental causes including biological attack, UV degradation, freezing, or thawing, or due to structural defects including cracks, movement, or distortion.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 420 0]>>/Prev 2692 0 R/First 2694 0 R/Last 2694 0 R/Count 1/Next 2695 0 R>>
endobj
2694 0 obj<</Title(1. Do not proceed with work in question until directed by Contracting Officer.)/Parent 2693 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 370 0]>>>>
endobj
2695 0 obj<</Title(D. Where Work requires existing features to be removed, cleaned, and reinstalled, perform operations without damage to material itself, to adjacent materials, or to substrate.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 345 0]>>/Prev 2693 0 R/Next 2696 0 R>>
endobj
2696 0 obj<</Title(E. Identify new or replacement materials and features with inconspicuous, permanent marks to distinguish from original materials. Record legend of identification marks and locations of these marks on Record Drawings.)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 308 0]>>/Prev 2695 0 R/Next 2697 0 R>>
endobj
2697 0 obj<</Title(F. When cleaning, match samples of existing materials that have been cleaned and identified for acceptable cleaning levels. Avoid over-cleaning to prevent damage. Use gentlest methods available. Initiate cleaning using hand cleaning methods before int...)/Parent 2686 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[2375 0 R/XYZ 69 258 0]>>/Prev 2696 0 R>>
endobj
2698 0 obj<</Type/Page/Parent 2894 0 R/Resources<</Font<</F1 2710 0 R/F2 2706 0 R/F3 2702 0 R>>/ExtGState<</GS7 2701 0 R/GS8 2700 0 R>>/ProcSet[/PDF/Text/ImageB/ImageC/ImageI]>>/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Contents 2699 0 R/Group<</Type/Group/S/Transparency/CS/DeviceRGB>>/Tabs/S/StructParents 0>>
